WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:09.170
Trick-shot artists Garrett Hilbert, Cody Jones,
Tyler Toney, and twins Coby and Cory Cotton

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:14.160
make up a little group known as Dude Perfect,
and they have one of the biggest channels

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.290
on YouTube.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:21.350
Dude Perfect is now so big that their channel
now has even more subscribers than the NFL,

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.579
NBA, MLB, and NHL combined.

00:00:24.579 --> 00:00:29.910
They have their own television show on CMT,
they’re sponsored by a wide range of major

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:35.730
companies, and they even have their own crazy
trick-shot factory in Frisco, Texas.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.120
They've transformed themselves into one of
the most successful brands to come from YouTube...but

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:45.580
it all started as five college roommates hanging
out in their backyard.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:46.910
Tyler Toney

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:49.710
The group specifically calls him "their leader."

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:54.420
Tyler Toney is the Dude on camera making the
majority of the group's trick shots, dating

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.780
back to their very first video.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:03.780
Born in Plano, Texas on March 24, 1989, Toney
did most of his growing up in nearby Prosper,

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.509
Texas, and spent much of his time in church.

00:01:06.509 --> 00:01:08.890
"Ever since I could remember I grew up in
a church.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:14.580
My earliest memories are being in church every
sunday, youth every wednesday, Awanas every

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.580
Monday night."

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:20.770
Toney also spent a lot of time on youth athletics,
and his efforts paid off.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:26.460
He stands 5-foot-9, but played quarterback,
developing a passing acumen that helps him

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.830
make many trick shots today.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:34.270
After high school, Toney attended Texas A&amp;M
and started looking for “some other Christian

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.390
guys to develop a friendship with.”

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.600
Toney credits that as the true start of Dude
Perfect.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.600
He already knew Garrett Hilbert from their
high school basketball team, and they soon

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.540
met the twins and Cody Jones.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:51.770
In 2009, they all moved into a house together
and put a basketball hoop in the backyard.

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:56.930
That's when they began betting sandwiches
on whether or not one of them could sink unusual

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:59.590
basketball shots in their backyard hoop.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:04.400
After some success, they decided to shoot
a video over two afternoons.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.220
This ended up becoming their first YouTube
video, "Backyard Edition."

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.980
Within a week it had over 100,000 views.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.029
Soon after, Good Morning America called for
an interview.

00:02:15.029 --> 00:02:20.430
Toney and Dude Perfect were on their way to
Internet superstardom and beyond.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:26.010
Along the way, Toney graduated from college
with a degree in wildlife and fisheries, got

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:31.029
a "real job" for awhile, and married Bethany
Briscoe, an elementary school teacher, in

00:02:31.029 --> 00:02:32.499
2011.

00:02:32.499 --> 00:02:33.930
Garrett Hilbert

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:39.930
The Purple Hoser, as he's known to fans, was
born in Texas on May 13, 1987.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:43.840
His dad's job moved him to California during
his early childhood.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.189
At some point, he found his way back to Prosper,
Texas before high school, because that's where

00:02:49.189 --> 00:02:52.180
he met Tyler Toney on the basketball team.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:57.230
Just like Toney, Hilbert was brought up in
a devout Christian family, but didn’t really

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.470
understand what that meant until sixth grade.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:02.409
"I never really understood what going to church
meant, you know.

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:07.579
I tried to pay attention, but pretty much
ended up scribbling on the sermon notes, just

00:03:07.579 --> 00:03:08.579
drawing.

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:14.280
And throughout all that, Christ was just slowly
telling me—about him and what he did for

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:15.400
me."

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:20.069
Hilbert went to Texas A&amp;M as an architecture
major, remained close with his high school

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:25.139
teammate Toney, and found his way into the
college house that brought them all together.

00:03:25.139 --> 00:03:29.949
He claims to be the one to have initially
bet Toney that he couldn't make a particular

00:03:29.949 --> 00:03:30.949
trick shot.

00:03:30.949 --> 00:03:31.949
"I bet him that he wouldn't make it.

00:03:31.949 --> 00:03:32.949
He obviously made it.

00:03:32.949 --> 00:03:34.629
I bought him lunch, and the rest is history."

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:40.129
Hilbert married in 2011, and he and his wife
have a baby boy together named Owen.

00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:42.019
Coby and Cory Cotton

00:03:42.019 --> 00:03:47.299
Coby is known as Twin #1 because he's one
minute older than Cory, a.k.a.

00:03:47.299 --> 00:03:48.299
Twin #2.

00:03:48.299 --> 00:03:54.859
Born on July 17, 1987, they grew up in Woodlands,
Texas, playing basketball, tennis, dodgeball,

00:03:54.859 --> 00:03:56.230
and ran cross country.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:04:01.019
"My dad is actually a pastor, and I know some
people have mixed feelings about pastors'

00:04:01.019 --> 00:04:05.919
kids, but for me my parents were never pushy
when it comes to Christianity.

00:04:05.919 --> 00:04:10.579
And they wanted me to make a decision on my
own whether I actually believed it."

00:04:10.579 --> 00:04:16.160
They both went to Texas A&amp;M as communications
majors and kept seeing Toney and Hilbert at

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:19.100
various Bible study groups on campus.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:24.850
Once the four bonded over sports and faith,
it was inevitable they'd all move in together.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:29.560
Not only are they the marketing geniuses in
the group, they also seem to be the technical

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:34.560
guys, being the point people for the group's
mobile game, website, and video editing.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:39.480
After they graduated from college, they went
to work for their father's church in Austin

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:42.330
before Dude Perfect really took off.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:47.400
During that period, Cory wrote a book about
the group called Go Big: Make Your Shot Count

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.950
in the Connected World.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:50.440
Cody Jones

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:56.430
Born in Plano, Texas on October 9, 1987, Jones
grew up going to church every Sunday with

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:58.670
his family, like the other Dudes.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:03.580
In high school, he played for the school's
basketball team before attending Texas A&amp;M

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:05.990
to study finance and real estate.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:10.810
But for a time, Cody Jones focused more on
basketball and girls than on religion.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:16.300
"Like any other teenager as I went into high
school, man, the things of this world kinda

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.530
captivated me."

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:22.120
Once Jones got back on the straight and narrow,
he met the Cotton twins while playing basketball

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:27.660
at the university rec center, and they asked
if he wanted to be the fifth roommate in their

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.660
house.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.400
After graduating from school, Jones married
his wife Allison and worked in commercial

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:36.660
real estate until their viral videos became
a full-time gig.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.820
And the rest, as they say, is history.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.070
Thanks for watching!

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.930
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:49.280
And leave us a comment to let us know which
YouTube celebs you’d like to hear more about...

